{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"camoflage-piscatory-hoopoe","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context\n\n`src/rebar/llm/review_workflows.py` (101 lines) is strangler-fig scaffolding for\na cutover that is now being cancelled rather than completed. Its own docstring\n(`:1-9`) states the design: express `review_ticket` as a one-step agent workflow\nand provide \"a parallel-run-and-diff that proves the workflow path yields the\nSAME findings as the legacy path … this adds the equivalent workflow path + the\ndiff that gates a future cutover.\"\n\nThe legacy path it diffs against is the single-pass review engine\n`operations._review_ticket_impl`, which ADR 0075 retired. There is no cutover to\ngate: the legacy side is being deleted, so a harness whose only job is to compare\nthe two paths has no remaining purpose. `diff_review_paths` (`:70`) is also one\nof the engine's few surviving callers (`:86`), so removing this module shrinks\nwhat the engine-deletion slice has to clear.\n\nThe module is fully self-contained. Measured on `origin/main` at\n`e2ed08b343a2be462de4433a93edbb5cbc062a52`, across `src tests docs scripts`\n(excluding `tests/fixtures/`, which contains the name only inside recorded\nagent-transcript text):\n\n- `review_ticket_workflow_doc` (`def :20`) — called only at `:54`, inside this module.\n- `run_review_ticket_as_workflow` (`def :39`) — called only at `:89`, inside this module.\n- `diff_review_paths` (`def :70`) — called only at `test_review_as_workflow.py:51`.\n- The module itself is imported exactly once outside itself:\n  `test_review_as_workflow.py:14`, `from rebar.llm import review_workflows as RW`.\n- `git grep -n 'review_workflows' -- docs` returns nothing, so no documentation\n  describes it.\n\nSo the whole module plus one test is the entire blast radius. No production code\noutside the file changes.\n\n## Approach\n\nDelete `src/rebar/llm/review_workflows.py` outright, delete the single test that\nexercises it, and drop the now-unused import. Record the removal in the release\nnotes.\n\nThis slice deliberately leaves the review engine in place — removing it is a\nlater slice. That keeps this change a pure, independently reviewable deletion of\none self-contained module.\n\n## Scope\n\nIn scope: `src/rebar/llm/review_workflows.py` (deleted),\n`tests/interfaces/store/test_review_as_workflow.py` (trimmed),\n`docs/release-notes.md` (entry added).\n\nOut of scope, verified rather than assumed:\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/operations.py` — the engine stays live through this slice. AC4\n  asserts it is still present. `default_reviewer_id` loses its `:52` caller here\n  but keeps its `operations.py:167` one, so it does **not** become dead yet.\n- `src/rebar/llm/workflow/` — the executor and the `RunnerAgentStep` bridge are\n  live, general machinery with many other users. This slice removes a *client* of\n  the bridge, not the bridge. AC3 asserts the bridge's own test survives.\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_review_as_workflow.py:57`\n  `test_public_review_ticket_entry_point_unchanged` — it calls the engine\n  directly (`:61`) and never touches `review_workflows`, so it belongs with the\n  engine's deletion, not here. It is left untouched.\n\n## Testing\n\nNo new tests. One test is deleted and two are kept. Locate them by name, not by\nline range.\n\n**Delete `test_review_workflow_equivalent_to_legacy`** (`def :45`). It exists\nsolely to assert the strangler-fig equivalence being retired: it calls\n`RW.diff_review_paths` (`:51`) and asserts `diff[\"equivalent\"] is True`,\n`legacy_findings == workflow_findings`, and\n`legacy_summary == workflow_summary == \"the summary\"` (`:52-54`). With\n`diff_review_paths` gone there is nothing left for it to assert.\n\n**Keep `test_runner_agent_step_bridge_runs_an_agent_workflow`** (`def :21`). It\ndoes **not** use `RW`: it builds its own workflow doc inline (`:24-36`) with\n`\"prompt\": \"code-quality\"` and calls `runs.run` directly (`:38`), asserting the\nbridge produced `findings[0][\"detail\"] == \"z\"` and `summary == \"ok\"`. That is\ncoverage of the surviving `RunnerAgentStep` bridge and must not be lost.\n\n**Also in that file:** delete the `from rebar.llm import review_workflows as RW`\nimport (`:14`) — it becomes unused and ruff will flag it. Leave the other imports\n(`rebar`, `FakeRunner`, `runs`, `Path`, `pytest`), which the two surviving tests\nstill use. Rewrite the module docstring (`:1-5`), whose current text — \"The\n``RunnerAgentStep`` path must match the legacy findings and summary while the\npublic entry point continues to use the legacy path\" — describes exactly the\nequivalence being deleted.\n\n**Release notes.** Add an entry to the unreleased section recording that\n`rebar.llm.review_workflows` and its three functions are removed, and why (the\nstrangler-fig cutover they gated is cancelled, not completed). Do not edit the\nexisting historical entries.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\nEach criterion is a single command whose stated result is the pass condition.\n\n- [ ] **AC1 — the module is gone.**\n      `test -e src/rebar/llm/review_workflows.py` exits non-zero.\n- [ ] **AC2 — nothing references it or its functions.**\n      `git grep -n 'review_workflows\\|diff_review_paths\\|run_review_ticket_as_workflow\\|review_ticket_workflow_doc' -- src tests docs scripts ':!tests/fixtures/' ':!docs/release-notes.md'`\n      prints nothing and exits 1. (`tests/fixtures/` holds the name inside recorded\n      transcript text, and the release-notes entry AC5 requires necessarily names\n      it; both would otherwise make this criterion unsatisfiable.)\n- [ ] **AC3 — the bridge test survives.**\n      `git grep -c 'def test_runner_agent_step_bridge_runs_an_agent_workflow' -- tests/interfaces/store/test_review_as_workflow.py`\n      prints `1`.\n- [ ] **AC4 — the engine is still present.**\n      `git grep -c 'def _review_ticket_impl' -- src/rebar/llm/operations.py` prints `1`.\n- [ ] **AC5 — the removal is recorded.**\n      `git grep -c 'review_workflows' -- docs/release-notes.md` prints at least `1`.\n- [ ] **AC6 — the trimmed module passes.**\n      `pytest tests/interfaces/store/test_review_as_workflow.py` exits 0 and\n      collects 2 tests, down from 3.\n- [ ] **AC7 — the suite is green.** `make verify` exits 0.\n","id":"1969-69f7-01f8-44ea","parent_id":"87d8-8bb6-5226-4a5b","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Delete the review_workflows strangler-fig module and its equivalence test"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793237389384933152,"uuid":"f8ddfc82-9f2c-4401-8f4c-92e969d03e5c"}